<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd">
<topic id="badges">
  <title>Badges</title>
  <shortdesc>Documentation and examples for badges, Bootstrap’s small count and labeling component.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Badges</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>ph</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section>
      <title>Example</title>
      <p>Badges scale to match the size of the immediate parent element by using relative font sizing and
          <xmlatt>em</xmlatt> units. As of v5, badges no longer have focus or hover styles for links.</p>
    </section>
    <bodydiv border="yes" padding="3">
      <section>
        <p outputclass="h1">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
        <p outputclass="h2">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
        <p outputclass="h3">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
        <p outputclass="h4">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
        <p outputclass="h5">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
        <p outputclass="h6">Example heading <badge>New</badge></p>
      </section>
    </bodydiv>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/badge/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/badge/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section>
      <title>Background colors</title>
      <p>Set a background-color with contrasting foreground color with Bootstrap’s <codeph
        >text-bg-{color}</codeph> helpers. Previously it was required to manually pair your choice of <xmlatt
        >outputclass</xmlatt> <codeph>text-{color}</codeph> and <codeph
        >bg-{color}</codeph> utilities for styling, which you still may use if you prefer.</p>
    </section>
    <bodydiv border="yes" padding="3">
      <p>
        <badge>Primary</badge>
        <badge color="secondary">Secondary</badge>
        <badge color="success">Success</badge>
        <badge color="danger">Danger</badge>
        <badge color="warning">Warning</badge>
        <badge color="info">Info</badge>
        <badge color="light">Light</badge>
        <badge color="dark">Dark</badge>
      </p>
    </bodydiv>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/badge/background-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/badge/background-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
  </body>
</topic>
